  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Against Plump Lady in Western Desert, Fang Yuan grows black bat wings that vanish like an illusion and shoot his body forward; she names the cast a movement killer move, and a second activation still fails to catch her light sand escape.",
      "chapters": [
        675
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_plump_lady",
        "reg_western_desert",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_killer_moves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later against Immortal Gu Dark Arrow he activates it by name again; the many mortal Gu that make up the move begin to wear down under repeated use, and after more than a hundred casts he still cannot shrug the arrows until Worldly Wave Trace finally carries him clear.",
      "chapters": [
        677
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_dark_arrow",
        "sys_mortal_gu",
        "gu_worldly_wave_trace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With icy drill stardust, light illusion bat wings, and hair armor in normal form, his battle strength sits at the upper tier of rank six.",
      "chapters": [
        681
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "During Hei Lou Lan’s flying blade noise tribulation he casts it with hair armor, then notes all three mortal moves have been pushed to their limits without ending the danger.",
      "chapters": [
        684
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_hei_lou_lan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Against mortal Gu Masters at an oasis he flaps the wings to fly like a meteor and close distance in a moment.",
      "chapters": [
        694
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After months of improvement work he upgrades the move by a great degree, but finishing the new version requires transplanting a real pair of bat wings onto his immortal zombie body from a bought bat desolate beast corpse.",
      "chapters": [
        712
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "physical-wing-form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The processed wings are yellow-brown and shorter than half an arm, yet they nearly double the speed boost and greatly extend flight duration because they are physical rather than phantom. Gu worms housed in the wings fire the modified movement killer move; he judges the old name no longer fits and renames it true solid bat wings. Treasure yellow heaven pricing for that modified move sits at about six immortal essence stones or more, with room to transplant up to three pairs of desolate-beast wings for about three times the speed of the original spread form.",
      "chapters": [
        713
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "physical-wing-form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Much later, when dodging an eagle attack, a phantom image flickers as light illusion bat wings appear again.",
      "chapters": [
        1055
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "physical-wing-form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
